{"source_organisation":"VITO (Flemish Institute for Technological Research), UrbClim model (De Ridder et al., 2015)","recommended_citations":["De Ridder, K., Lauwaet, D., Maiheu, B. (2015). UrbClim - A fast urban boundary layer climate model. Urban Climate 12, 21–48. doi:10.1016/j.uclim.2015.01.001","Souverijns, N. et al. (2026). 100m climate and heat stress data up to 2100 for 142 cities around the globe. Data in Brief 65, 112497. doi:10.1016/j.dib.2026.112497"],"method":"Daily maximum WBGT is pooled across June–August seasons for 2008–2017. Reported per tree: the committed reference day's value, the seasonal mean, maximum and 90th percentile, the mean number of June–August days per season at or above 26.0 °C, and where the reference day ranks inside the pooled June–August distribution.","interpretation_boundary":"This daily-maximum WBGT archive is from the same UrbClim model family and 100 m grid as the committed ranking raster, but it reports °C daily maxima while that raster is a normalized 0–100 indicator for a 24-hour mean scenario. It can test sensitivity to heat-period choice, but its values are not interchangeable with the raster and it does not replace the ranking input. The 2008–2017 window cannot show future climate change.","archive_urls":["https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2008.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2009.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2010.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2011.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2012.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2013.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2014.nc","https://provide.marvin.vito.be/ftp/compressed_daily/Brussels/WBGT_year_daily_max_2015.nc"